invariant: INV-65
file: widemul.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x25519-adx
reason: widemul_x25519_cpu runs x25519_adx.c under the multiply bit alone,
  whatever CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX says, so a session on a CPU without BMI2 or ADX
  dies of SIGILL at its first shared secret. On a CPU with them every byte
  stays right, so no vector notices. bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the
  call into x25519_adx.c under the multiply bit alone, and the qemu lane
  runs it for x86-64, the one architecture whose widemul.h holds the test.

--- old
    if (widemul_native(widemul) && (cpu & CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX) != 0) {
--- new
    if (widemul_native(widemul)) {
